gomodel:6ab067da00006813
        a                      owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment           "OXM enabler = GCG peptide chain UniProtKB:P01275-PRO_0000011255 (aa 53-89). OXM->GLP1R IDA from cAMP and BRET assays in GLP-1R-expressing cells (PMID:27315480 full text; PMID:17395766). GLP1R part of AC-activating GPCR pathway: OXM cAMP blocked by adenylyl cyclase inhibitors (PMID:27315480, Fig S1)." , "Not modelled: beta-arrestin 1/2 and GRK2 recruitment and arrestin contribution to pERK1/2 (PMID:17395766, 27315480, 38360293); OXM reduction of beta-cell apoptosis (PMID:18669601); OXM action on GCGR. Upstream OXM production by L cells: see gomodel:6ab067da00005905." , "Insulin: native OXM infusion increased glucose-dependent insulin secretion rate in obese humans with and without T2DM (PMID:29545266, abstract only) -> IDA on the OXM pathway; GLP1R pathway part of GSIS and GLP1R in beta-cell plasma membrane are IC. GLP1R-dependence of OXM-stimulated insulin secretion shown in mouse Glp1r-/- islets and INS-1 cells (PMID:18669601, abstract only), not used as evidence in this human model." , "Downstream cAMP units (added 2026-10-13, revised 2026-10-14): GLP1R -> GNAS (Gs) -> adenylate cyclase -> cAMP -> PRKACA and RAPGEF4/Epac2. Adenylate cyclase enabled by generic protein (PR:000000001): the ADCY isoform acting downstream of GLP1R in human beta cells is not established (ADCY5 couples glucose but not GLP-1 to insulin secretion in human islets, PMID:24740569; mouse Adcy8 KO, PMID:25403481, did not test GLP-1). Adenylate cyclase positively regulates PKA and Epac2 via cAMP (has output / has small molecule activator). Downstream steps not tested with OXM; several edges are ISS from mouse MGI orthologs." ;
        lego:conforms_to_gpad  false ;
        lego:modelstate        "development" ;
        dc:contributor         "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5283-6593" ;
        dc:date                "2026-10-14" ;
        dc:title               "Oxyntomodulin-GLP1R stimulated insulin secretion (Human)" ;
        pav:providedBy         "http://geneontology.org" , "https://www.uniprot.org" ;
        owl:versionIRI         gomodel:6ab067da00006813 ;
        biolink:in_taxon       obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

